      "side": 1,
      "message": "With the actor stopping right after its request, this timeout can only fire when there is nothing to cancel, so write-transaction-idle-timeout (described as \"cancelled automatically\" in NetconfTopologyManager) silently stops covering forwarded RESTCONF writes, and an abandoned edit leaves the candidate locked for the next transaction to commit. Could we drop the receive timeout here entirely, adjust that description, and track abandoned-transaction cleanup? (maybe in a follow-up ticket?)",
